00:09:17.933 --> 00:09:19.559
who I know, who I've never met in person,

00:09:19.559 --> 00:09:21.352
but they comment on all the videos,

00:09:21.352 --> 00:09:24.068
they share, they tweet the videos out.

00:09:24.068 --> 00:09:26.071
They add as much value as they can

00:09:26.071 --> 00:09:27.974
to the Believe Nation community.

00:09:27.974 --> 00:09:29.762
If they needed me for something,

00:09:29.762 --> 00:09:31.403
if they wanted me to check
out their business plan,

00:09:31.403 --> 00:09:33.149
if they wanted to hop
on a quick phone call

00:09:33.149 --> 00:09:34.877
to talk about something,

00:09:34.877 --> 00:09:36.066
I would say yes.

00:09:36.066 --> 00:09:37.464
Because they've added so much value.

00:09:37.464 --> 00:09:38.869
Ten years ago it wasn't possible.

00:09:38.869 --> 00:09:40.694
It wasn't possible to
reach out to that person

00:09:40.694 --> 00:09:42.179
and get that connection.

00:09:42.179 --> 00:09:44.158
And understand that, people
who have had success,

00:09:44.158 --> 00:09:46.445
for the most part, want
to give back as well.

00:09:46.445 --> 00:09:48.240
Because somewhere along the line,

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:49.616
somebody helped them.

00:09:49.616 --> 00:09:51.480
Right, for me mentors helped me get to

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:53.086
where I'm at.

00:09:53.086 --> 00:09:55.178
So, I want to help other people.

00:09:55.178 --> 00:09:57.562
It's really fulfilling
to give back and help.

00:09:57.562 --> 00:09:59.703
But, again, make sure that it's the people

00:09:59.703 --> 00:10:01.935
who are actually going to do the work.

00:10:01.935 --> 00:10:03.574
And so separating yourself out

00:10:03.574 --> 00:10:05.470
as being the hustler,

00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:06.841
of being the person who will grind it.

00:10:06.841 --> 00:10:08.267
Who will take the advice,

00:10:08.267 --> 00:10:10.878
a little bit of advice, and
just go an push hard on it,

00:10:10.878 --> 00:10:12.166
and achieve some success,

00:10:12.166 --> 00:10:13.740
then come back and ask for
a little bit more advice,

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:15.215
is really important.

00:10:15.215 --> 00:10:17.328
But, the access has never been easier

00:10:17.328 --> 00:10:18.925
to get on somebody's radar

00:10:18.925 --> 00:10:21.693
who could give you meaningful
advice in a conversation.

00:10:21.693 --> 00:10:25.943
(heavy drum techno music)

00:10:25.943 --> 00:10:27.392
And number seven is do both.

00:10:27.392 --> 00:10:29.524
You don't have to do one or the other.

00:10:29.524 --> 00:10:32.078
You don't have to have a
career or start a business.

00:10:32.078 --> 00:10:33.628
You could do both in parallel.

00:10:33.628 --> 00:10:35.198
And I actually recommend it.

00:10:35.198 --> 00:10:36.610
I think if your long term goal

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:39.230
is to be an entrepreneur,
and have your own business,

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:40.997
then go work for an entrepreneur.

00:10:40.997 --> 00:10:42.538
Don't go work at some big bank,

00:10:42.538 --> 00:10:44.109
go work for an entrepreneur

00:10:44.109 --> 00:10:45.806
who is a little bit ahead of you.

00:10:45.806 --> 00:10:47.776
Who has 10 employees, who
you could see yourself being

00:10:47.776 --> 00:10:49.225
in three to five years.

00:10:49.225 --> 00:10:52.117
Go work for them, and take on
as much as you can to learn,

00:10:52.117 --> 00:10:53.830
not just your one, specific role.

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:56.054
But, get close to the
entrepreneur founder.

00:10:56.054 --> 00:10:57.582
Learn as much as you can.

00:10:57.582 --> 00:10:58.481
Understand the industry.

00:10:58.481 --> 00:10:59.727
Understand how their business works.

00:10:59.727 --> 00:11:01.556
You're essentially getting
paid to go to school.

00:11:01.556 --> 00:11:02.411
Right?

00:11:02.411 --> 00:11:04.130
Right now, you're paying to go to school.

00:11:04.130 --> 00:11:05.571
You're getting paid now to learn

00:11:05.571 --> 00:11:06.955
how an industry works.

00:11:06.955 --> 00:11:10.336
And at the same time,
you start your business.

00:11:10.336 --> 00:11:12.275
You start your side hustle.

00:11:12.275 --> 00:11:14.117
You're off grinding trying
to make this thing work.

00:11:14.117 --> 00:11:15.645
And everything you learn from your job

00:11:15.645 --> 00:11:17.495
you're now applying to your business.

00:11:17.495 --> 00:11:19.151
That's why it's so important to get a job

00:11:19.151 --> 00:11:20.634
where you're going to learn.

00:11:20.634 --> 00:11:22.037
Yes, you get paid, but
you're going to learn.

00:11:22.037 --> 00:11:23.868
Because it makes you
a better entrepreneur,

00:11:23.868 --> 00:11:25.334
it makes you a better human being.

00:11:25.334 --> 00:11:26.658
And the things you're
going to learn over here,

00:11:26.658 --> 00:11:28.326
you're going to bring to your business.

00:11:28.326 --> 00:11:29.627
You're going to start to build it up.

00:11:29.627 --> 00:11:31.011
And when you get to the point where

00:11:31.011 --> 00:11:32.523
either you're not learning
as much as you used to

00:11:32.523 --> 00:11:35.219
at that job you had, or
where your own business

00:11:35.219 --> 00:11:36.728
is getting to the point where

00:11:36.728 --> 00:11:39.538
it's sustaining you, you
can afford to quit the job,

00:11:39.538 --> 00:11:41.772
then you can go all in on your business.

00:11:41.772 --> 00:11:43.583
I wouldn't approach any situation

00:11:43.583 --> 00:11:45.807
where it's either one or the other.

00:11:45.807 --> 00:11:48.076
Often, the answer to those,

00:11:48.076 --> 00:11:50.707
should I do this or should I do this,

00:11:50.707 --> 00:11:52.498
often the answer is yes.

00:11:52.498 --> 00:11:53.822
It's do both.

00:11:53.822 --> 00:11:55.428
Embrace the genius of the and.

00:11:55.428 --> 00:11:56.261
(swish)

00:11:56.261 --> 00:11:57.347
So those are my seven reasons why

00:11:57.347 --> 00:11:59.739
millennials should start
their business today.

00:11:59.739 --> 00:12:01.371
I'd love to know what do you guys think?

00:12:01.371 --> 00:12:02.585
What was your favorite rule?

00:12:02.585 --> 00:12:03.742
What resonated the most with you?

00:12:03.742 --> 00:12:05.153
Did I miss some?

00:12:05.153 --> 00:12:06.486
Is there and eight, nine, 10 that

00:12:06.486 --> 00:12:07.911
you guys want to add to the list?

00:12:07.911 --> 00:12:09.042
Let me know.

00:12:09.042 --> 00:12:09.924
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:12:09.924 --> 00:12:11.310
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:12.826
Finally, I want to give a quick shout out

00:12:12.826 --> 00:12:14.424
109 Innovations.

00:12:14.424 --> 00:12:15.997
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:12:15.997 --> 00:12:17.506
"Your One Word."

00:12:17.506 --> 00:12:18.964
It really, really,
really means a lot to me,

00:12:18.964 --> 00:12:20.707
and I hope you're enjoying it.

00:12:20.707 --> 00:12:22.540
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:23.908
I believe in you.

00:12:23.908 --> 00:12:25.845
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:12:25.845 --> 00:12:28.080
And whatever your one word is,

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:30.389
much love, I'll see you soon.

00:12:30.389 --> 00:12:31.312
(deep swish)

00:12:31.312 --> 00:12:32.624
(thunder clap)

